WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.379
All right, let's get into audience questions
for the week.

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:05.280
The first one, very, very ripe for people
both

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.880
have been very angry with me.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.769
The question is, Hey David, why are you ignoring
Tulsi Gabard all the time?

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:18.720
Which is just so funny because I, I talk about
Tulsi Gabard as much as I talk about any of

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.199
the other one percenters.

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:26.160
Uh, except I'd say Andrew Yang because Andrew
Yang has been on our show three times.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.280
Tulsi is welcome anytime and I'd be glad to
interview her on the program.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.430
I talked about Marianne Williamson a little
bit after the second debate because I thought

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.969
she actually did notably well in that debate,
but still big picture, especially after finding

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:43.670
out that she was, uh, offering new age woo
stuff to her campaign list, which is crazy.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.360
I mean, she's just another one of these one
percenters that's going nowhere.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.039
The problem I don't think is that I am talking
about Tulsi Gabbert not enough.

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.079
She's basically getting the same attention
from me as the other zero to one percenters

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:58.010
who are not going to last much longer.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:03.629
The problem is that there is a cult of personality
around Tulsi that makes people see that.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:10.329
When I don't talk about Amy Klobuchar or I
don't talk about Kirsten Gillibrand, it doesn't

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:15.209
warrant emails to me or complaints or any
kind of investigation into what my biases

00:01:15.209 --> 00:01:18.210
are, but not talking about Tulsi.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.659
There definitely is something going on there.

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:25.469
This is again what I was talking about a couple
of weeks ago when I said I sort of self-censor

00:01:25.469 --> 00:01:30.679
on some issues because there no upside and
in this case it's not even that it's, there's

00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:36.020
no specific focus or lack of focus on Tulsi
on this program.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:42.700
There are lots of people in my audience who
see everything through Tulsi colored glasses.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.889
I guess I would say where when I do talk about
Tulsi Gabard, if it's anything short of completely

00:01:48.889 --> 00:01:54.520
glowing and everything is just so amazing
that Tulsi does, I'm some kind of, you know,

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.619
anti Tulsi shill or democratic this or that.

00:01:57.619 --> 00:01:59.630
Who even knows what the argument is.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:05.329
If I don't talk about Tulsi, the absence of
discussions of Tulsi are what is the problem

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:09.890
even though I'm also barely talking about
any of the other candidates that are, uh,

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:13.579
polling zero to one or zero to one and a half.

00:02:13.579 --> 00:02:15.629
So this is an example of what I was talking
about.

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:19.910
No matter what I do, if I talk about her in
anything but the most glowing terms, if I

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.939
don't talk about her no matter what, I'm clearly
doing something wrong.

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:26.660
Let me say it in completely clear terms.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:36.049
I have no particular favor or disfavor for
Tulsi Gabard compared to John Delaney or Hickenlooper

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:38.420
or Marianne Williamson or whoever.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.420
I mean, okay.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.700
I find the new age guru stuff weird with Marianne
Williamson.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.799
I see Tulsi Gabbert as a candidate who like
all of the candidates, I can find things I

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.840
agree with her.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.840
On.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.110
There are things I disagree on, but I basically
pay attention to her in proportion to what

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.540
I believe is the appropriate amount of attention
that should be paid and given that she is

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.499
pulling zero to one and a half percent, given
that she is not done particularly well in

00:03:01.499 --> 00:03:06.689
the debates, given that she's not come up
with any particularly interesting policy,

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:10.439
for example, the way that I think Andrew Yang
has, that's all it is.

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:14.959
I'm just talking about her in proportion to
how important I think she is in this race.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:17.230
You can disagree with me about that.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.230
You can tell me David.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:22.870
No, here's why Tulsi really is the person
that even though she's polling zero to one,

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:27.129
like all these other people, you should be
talking about way more than we can have a

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:31.379
conversation, but just saying, David, the
fact that you are quote, ignoring Tulsi Gabbert

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:32.659
is the problem.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:33.659
This is laughable.

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:37.889
This is the exact cult of personality stuff
that I've been talking about when I talk about

00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:42.810
all of these issues that if you don't say
the right thing, there is a sliver of the

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.769
left that will absolutely go crazy and attack
you.

